WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:08.967
♪♪

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:11.345
Gaal:
When I was a child, at the edge
of the galaxy...

00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:13.096
♪♪

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:17.351
Gaal: 
I heard stories about a man who
could forecast the future.

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:18.977
♪♪

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:22.272
Gaal:
But the story remained dark to
me until many years later.

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:24.233
♪♪

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:25.984
Gaal:
Until it became my story.

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:31.907
♪♪

00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:34.076
Gaal:
Until it became the only story.

00:00:34.076 --> 00:00:36.245
♪♪

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:38.413
Hari:
You're familiar with my work,
psychohistory?

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:40.624
Every mathematician has read
your theory.

00:00:40.624 --> 00:00:41.833
-It's not a theory.

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:46.129
Hari:
It's the future of mankind
expressed in numbers.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:49.007
Hari:
And the empire won't like the
future I predict.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:51.218
♪♪

00:00:51.218 --> 00:00:55.013
History is littered with
charlatans and false messiahs.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:56.265
♪♪

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:57.516
We should kill them.

00:00:57.516 --> 00:00:58.809
♪♪

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:01.561
Brother Day:
We can murder the man, but what
about the movement, brother?

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.688
♪♪

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:05.148
Martyrs tend to have a long
half-life.

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:07.651
♪♪

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:09.069
Gaal:
His math was right.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.779
Gaal:
The empire is dying.

00:01:10.779 --> 00:01:12.239
♪♪

00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:13.657
Wars will be endless.

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.033
(Men yelling)

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.619
Hari:
A thousand worlds reduced to
cinders.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:24.876
♪♪

00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:26.712
Hari:
Change is frightening.

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:27.713
♪♪

00:01:27.713 --> 00:01:29.131
Hari:
Especially to those in power.

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:30.757
♪♪

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.093
Hari:
But we can soften the fall.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.470
♪♪

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.888
So what's the plan?

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:38.682
♪♪

00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:40.600
Hari:
Many years from now,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.061
Hari:
if humanity is to climb from the
ashes,

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:44.062
♪♪

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:47.899
Hari:
the coming generations will need
the knowledge to build upon,

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:48.817
a foundation.

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:51.069
♪♪

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:52.738
Gaal:
We must preserve only the most

00:01:52.738 --> 00:01:55.407
Gaal:
essential pieces of
civilization.

00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:57.284
♪♪

00:01:57.284 --> 00:01:58.785
Gaal:
Deciding what is remembered, 

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.078
♪♪

00:02:00.078 --> 00:02:00.704
Gaal:
what is forgotten.

00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:03.957
♪♪

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.584
Man:
We are now staring down the
barrel...

00:02:05.584 --> 00:02:06.793
♪♪

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.794
Man:
...of a crisis.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.714
♪♪

00:02:10.714 --> 00:02:11.882
This is the plan.

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:16.511
♪♪

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.096
Gaal:
We're not turning around now.

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:35.947
♪♪

